				41
			],
			"Message": "fix(Cocoon): Forward WebviewView options to Mountain and polish logging\n\nThe `CreateWebviewViewBuilder` previously stored webview options in a static object without forwarding them to the Mountain backend. This caused the workbench webview to render with default security settings (e.g., `enableScripts: false`), preventing extension UIs that rely on scripts or forms from functioning correctly.\n\nIntroduce a reactive `options` getter/setter in the builder. The setter now captures any user-provided configuration and immediately forwards it to Mountain via the `webview.setOptions` gRPC command. This ensures the native webview instance respects the extension's declared capabilities. Additionally, standardize trace logging by ensuring all stdout writes in the trace block explicitly terminate with a newline character to prevent log stream corruption.\n\nAlso update `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` to use bullet points for feature lists and standardize markdown formatting for consistency. Rebuild all `Target/` artifacts and refresh the `RouteManifest` timestamp to 2026-05-15T23:58:27Z.",
			"SHA": "a2ff9185f340ef69685a5b7b15c5ee244e56fe9c"
		}
